---
import ProfileLinks from "../components/ProfileLinks.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import PhotoStrip from "../components/PhotoStrip.astro";
import papers from "../data/papers.json";
import "../interior.css";

const journal = papers.filter((paper) => paper.type.startsWith("Journal"));
const preprints = papers
  .filter((paper) => paper.type.startsWith("Preprint"))
  .sort((first, second) => second.details.localeCompare(first.details));
const publishedAndPosted = [...journal, ...preprints];
const related = papers.filter(
  (paper) =>
    paper.type.startsWith("Working") || paper.type.startsWith("Public"),
);
---

<Layout
  title="Quantum physicist"
  description="Souvik Ghosh’s quantum computing experiments, independent theory, Vishwa Vigyan Labs projects, papers and academic CV."
>
  <article class="folio science" id="science">
    <header>
      <span class="stamp">Souvik Ghosh / Research</span>
      <h1>Quantum physicist</h1>
      <p class="intro">
        I work on experiments in quantum computing. I also do independent
        research into how electrons move through small devices.
      </p>
      <div class="research-links">
        <a class="cv" href="/Souvik-Ghosh-CV.pdf" download>
          Download my CV <small>PDF ↓</small>
        </a>
        <a href="#papers">Read my papers</a>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="folio-row">
      <h2>At the lab</h2>
      <div>
        <p>
          My experimental work is at the Quantum Circuit Lab in the Department
          of Physics at National Sun Yat-sen University, Taiwan. My advisor is
          Assoc. Prof. Kuei-Lin Chiu.
        </p>
        <p>
          I cool small circuits to temperatures close to absolute zero and use
          microwaves to measure their response. Those measurements tell us how a
          qubit behaves inside a device.
        </p>
        <PhotoStrip
          items={[
            ["fridge-work", "Working on the dilution refrigerator"],
            ["under-plate", "Beneath the lowest plate"],
            ["circuit-detail", "A circuit assembly in hand"],
          ]}
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="folio-row">
      <h2>Independent theory</h2>
      <div>
        <p>
          In a chain of coupled sites, what makes a quantum state spread out,
          gather at an edge or stay in one place? I study that question in
          non-Hermitian SSH chains with quasiperiodic modulation. A separate
          preprint uses related mathematics to study why a neural network can
          become unstable during training.
        </p>
        <p>
          My other theoretical work follows electrons through small conductors,
          with a focus on Landauer conductance and local partial density of
          states. My independent research lives under Vishwa Vigyan Labs.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="folio-row">
      <h2>Vishwa Vigyan Labs</h2>
      <div>
        <p>
          My independent work has its own home at Vishwa Vigyan. The project
          pages include models you can try and distinguish published work from
          open questions.
        </p>
        <ul class="project-list">
          <li>
            <a href="https://vishwavigyan.com/non-hermitian.html">
              Non-Hermitian systems
            </a>{" "}
            — why a wave can gather at the edge of a chain.
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href="https://vishwavigyan.com/quantum-time-lab.html">
              Quantum Time Lab
            </a>{" "}
            — an ongoing study of transport and the interpretation of time.
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href="https://vishwavigyan.com/bigbang-atlas.html">
              Big Bang Atlas
            </a>{" "}
            — an early exploration of cosmology with Prof. Prosenjit Singha Deo.
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href="https://vishwavigyan.com/quantum-ai.html">Quantum AI</a> —
            experiments and an interactive illustration of a driven qubit.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/inventor/">
          For telescope and engineering work, visit my inventor profile →
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="folio-row" id="papers">
      <h2>Papers</h2>
      <div>
        <ol class="bibliography">
          {publishedAndPosted.map((paper) => (
            <li>
              <span class="folio-meta">{paper.type}</span>
              <h3>
                <a href={paper.url!}>{paper.title}</a>
              </h3>
              <p>{paper.authors}</p>
              <p class="record">{paper.details}</p>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>
        <details>
          <summary>Related writing and work in progress</summary>
          <ul class="bibliography">
            {related.map((item) => (
              <li>
                <span class="folio-meta">{item.type}</span>
                <h3>
                  {item.url ? <a href={item.url}>{item.title}</a> : item.title}
                </h3>
                <p>{item.authors}</p>
                <p class="record">{item.details}</p>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="folio-row">
      <h2>Research background</h2>
      <div>
        <p>
          I completed my M.Sc. in Physics at Adamas University in 2024,
          specializing in condensed matter. My dissertation studied how a
          quasiperiodic layer changes reflection at a junction between a metal
          and a superconductor.
        </p>
        <p>
          My earlier research at the S. N. Bose National Centre for Basic
          Sciences in Kolkata focused on mesoscopic transport.
        </p>
        <p>
          For research enquiries, write to{" "}
          <a href="mailto:founder@vishwavigyan.com">founder@vishwavigyan.com</a>
          .
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <ProfileLinks related={["inventor", "wellness-rd"]} />
  </article>
</Layout>
<style>
  .research-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1.4rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  .science a.cv {
    display: inline-flex;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 0.65rem 1rem;
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .cv small {
    font: 500 0.7rem var(--mono);
    color: var(--sky);
  }
  .cv:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  .bibliography {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .bibliography li {
    padding-bottom: 1.2rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 25%, transparent);
  }
  .bibliography h3 {
    font-size: clamp(1.18rem, 2.5vw, 1.55rem);
  }
  .bibliography p {
    margin: 0.15em 0;
  }
  .bibliography .record {
    font-size: 0.88em;
  }
  summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    padding: 0.5rem 0;
  }
  details[open] .bibliography {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }
</style>
